{
  "study": "Embedded against remote calculation (K, B24), 2026-10-14",
  "stack": {
    "revision": "36da1c8 (bench/solver-profiling, L) plus the solver pool background limit from bench/embedded-vs-remote",
    "shape": "deploy/vm rehearsal: scheduler-booking (role booking, 2 CPUs, 2 GiB, capacity 2, confirm slots 1), scheduler-daily (role daily, 2 CPUs, 2 GiB, capacity 2, background limit 2), scheduler-proxy nginx, scheduler-db Postgres 16; routing service on the CH graph (no CPU limit), Omaha map 2026-10-13; remote runs add solver-service (profile remote-solver, 4 CPUs, 4 GiB, http://solver-service:8002 on the private network) with SCHEDULER_CALCULATION_MODE=REMOTE on both pools",
    "jvm": "eclipse-temurin:25-jre, -XX:MaxRAMPercentage=75, G1",
    "acceptance": "from the plan: remote p95 at most 1.05 times embedded",
    "decision": "Embedded stays the default. Remote is a lever for a daily pool (same proposal latency, the solve CPU moves to the pool), not for booking (1.5 times the search latency from up to three round trips per search). A solver pool needs SOLVER_CAPACITY equal to the replicas summed search capacities and a background limit covering the daily replicas (new setting SOLVER_BACKGROUND_LIMIT, default every slot); with the previous defaults (capacity 2, one daily at a time) most daily proposals answered 503."
  },
